# NASA Exoplanet Discovery Dashboard

Full-stack app that visualizes NASA public exoplanet data using:
- React + TypeScript + Vite frontend
- ASP.NET Core Web API backend (C#)
- Retry logic for transient upstream failures

## Project Structure

- frontend: React TypeScript dashboard
- backend: .NET Web API proxy to NASA Exoplanet Archive TAP endpoint

## Data Source

This implementation uses the NASA Exoplanet Archive TAP sync endpoint:
- https://exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu/TAP/sync

Note: This endpoint does not require a NASA API key. You selected DEMO_KEY initially, but for this data source no key is needed.

## Backend Features

- Endpoint: GET /api/exoplanets/tap
- Query passthrough model (single endpoint)
- Retries on transient failures:
  - HTTP 429
  - HTTP 5xx
  - network/timeouts
- Exponential backoff with jitter
- Configurable options via appsettings.json

## Frontend Features

- On-demand fetch button
- Filters:
  - Start year
  - End year
  - Discovery method
  - Host star name contains text
- Visualizations:
  - Discovery timeline line chart
  - Discovery method comparison bars
- KPI cards:
  - Total planets
  - Distinct host stars
  - Top method
  - Peak discovery year

## Run Locally

### 1) Start backend

From backend folder:

dotnet run --urls http://localhost:5099

### 2) Start frontend

From frontend folder:

npm run dev

The frontend runs on http://localhost:5173 and proxies /api requests to http://localhost:5099.

## Build

### Backend

dotnet build

### Frontend

npm run build

## Configuration

Backend settings are in backend/appsettings.json under NasaApi:
- TapBaseUrl
- TimeoutSeconds
- MaxRetries
- InitialBackoffMilliseconds
